# Soma Messages linked to the Mac's iMessage service (0.6+). Against the service's DEMO on the Mac Pro: sample
# chats only, nothing of Boss's; every send gets a fake reply 2 s later. The token below is the demo's own.
shell cmd statusbar collapse
key HOME
# A clean start: not linked yet, no contacts answer.
shell pm clear dev.omalauncher.messages
shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d 'soma-messages://link?url=http%3A%2F%2F100.120.219.46%3A8765&token=BON7avwraojOZCR1WT8sLWZg9WTx0RFaqeR3udg1kzA' dev.omalauncher.messages
wait 2500
# The owner says yes to the Mac by name before anything goes to it.
expect Get your iMessages from 100.120.219.46?
shot link-dialog
tap Link
wait 1500
# Names come from the phone's contacts, with his OK; the Mac's names stand in when the phone has none.
tap Allow | ALLOW
wait 4000
expect Weekend
expect Ana Demo
absent OpenBubbles
shot inbox-from-the-mac
tap Weekend
wait 2000
expect Look at this
expect 1 Photo
expect from your Mac
shot group-with-photo-card
key BACK
wait 800
tap Ana Demo
wait 2000
# A threaded reply from the Mac shows the message it answers.
expect Perfect, see you there
expect You: Yes! 7pm
shot reply-quote
tap Message
type walk test from the Fold
tap Send
wait 1000
expect walk test from the Fold
# The Mac's copy takes the place of the one sent from here (once, not twice), and the demo answers.
wait 3500
expect Demo reply to: walk test from the Fold
shot sent-and-answered
# The Mac stopped: the inbox says so and keeps what it has.
[phone] With the real service on the MacBook: link from the phone-link file (Taildropped), chats and names are Boss's own, one plain-text send to a chat he picks arrives on his other devices, a reply from him shows within seconds.
[phone] Mac locked: one plain text and one tapback (later slice) still go; note which don't.
